<title>HUNGARY: BUDAPEST BSE SUSPENDS PANNON-FLAX -TRADERS.</title>
<headline>BUDAPEST BSE SUSPENDS PANNON-FLAX -TRADERS.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Budapest Stock Exchange suspended trading in the shares of textile industrial company Pannon-Flax on Tuesday following too rapid an intraday rise after the release its 1996 results, traders said.</p>
<p>Pannon-Flax shares opened at 570 forints and rallied 20 percent to a year-high of 660 forints, triggering its suspension about a quarter hour before spot trading closes, they said.</p>
<p>Pannon-Flax released its 1996 results this morning and said that its 80.2 million forint pre-tax profit represented 267.4 percent of the 1995 figures.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
